Firn is a deeply-inspired rewrite of the fisherman installer, and
incorporates code copied from or derived from that lineage:

  - tuna-os/fisherman        (original project)
  - projectbluefin/fisherman (upstream continuation)
  - frostyard/fisherman      (frostyard fork)

Fisherman is licensed GPL-3.0-only. Files copied or substantially
derived from fisherman retain a provenance comment at the top of the
file identifying their origin.

Firn also ports logic from the snosi native installer
(frostyard/snosi, shared/native-installer), part of the same
frostyard project.

Rationale and attribution policy: docs/adr/0003-rewrite-fisherman-as-firn.md

The graphical installer, firn-gui (the gui/ module), is built with
frostui (frostyard/frostui, MIT) and carries what frostui embeds:
the Inter typeface (https://rsms.me/inter/), copyright 2016 The Inter
Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
(https://openfontlicense.org), and icons of Lucide (https://lucide.dev),
under the ISC license, with those Lucide derived from Feather also under
the MIT license. frostui's NOTICE, fonts/OFL.txt and icons/LICENSE hold
the full texts. Rationale: docs/adr/0022-draw-the-graphical-installer-with-frostui.md
